    const list = goalieList(), G = ST.goalieRun; return `<div class="panel"><h2>Goalies: how each would do</h2><p class="sub">Each goalie plays the same simulated games, on the same seeds and inputs, with only the goalie changed. Current rotation’s goalie is the comparison point. No game validation applies.</p><div class="row" style="margin-bottom:8px"><button class="go" id="runGoalies" ${ST.busy ? 'disabled' : ''}>Simulate all ${list.length} goalies</button></div>${G ? `<div class="wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Goalie</th><th>Saves</th><th>Goals allowed</th><th>Save %</th><th>W&L win</th><th>vs current</th><th>SE</th><th>Read</th><th class="l">Why</th></tr></thead><tbody>${G.rows.map(r => `<tr><td>${esc(nameOf(r.id))}${r.current ? ' (current)' : ''}</td><td>${num(r.saves)}</td><td>${num(r.ga)}</td><td>${pct(r.savePct)}</td><td>${pct(r.win)}</td><td>${r.current ? '—' : (100 * r.diff >= 0 ? '+' : '') + (100 * r.diff).toFixed(1) + ' pts'}</td><td>${r.current ? '—' : (100 * r.se).toFixed(1)}</td><td>${esc(r.read)}</td><td class="l reason">${esc(r.why)}</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div><ul class="note"><li>Highest projected among these goalies. Not proof of who will play best.</li><li>Every goalie’s rate is pulled toward the team average, with an assumed weight of ${G.k} shots, because the samples are small. It isn’t adjusted for the quality of shots faced.</li><li>${G.games.toLocaleString()} games each, seed ${G.seed}. Sources: ${esc(G.sources)}.</li></ul>` : ''}</div>`;
